ors","Wax Dr","Waxdoctor"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/785-Wax-Doctor","type":"artist","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/label/109/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"109","image":"https://i.discogs.com/6Ak_MtJpsdovwj3vv2S8TG6AL8JuDVxNBa13-k-TvlM/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTEwOS0x/NTY1MDE5MDc0LTU2/NjcucG5n.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/IhtVRHLYx9LPPooX9W5QCipDyxaG60OgQUOD17HHvvo/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTEwOS0x/NTY1MDE5MDc0LTU2/NjcucG5n.jpeg","profile":"Label Code: LC 12885\nNinja Tune is a record label and global distributor based in London, England (with a satellite office in Los Angeles for US & Canada business), created in 1990 by the duo known as [a=Coldcut]. Coldcut were pioneers of the emerging hip-hop/electro scene in the eighties. Inspired by a visit to Japan, [a=Matt Black] & [a=Jonathan More] (Coldcut) primarily created Ninja Tune to act as a vehicle by which they could release music of a more underground nature, free from the restraints placed on artists by major labels (the same restraints that were put on them via their brief stints with [l=Arista] and [l=Big Life]).\n\nThe first four volumes of [a=DJ Food] - Jazz Brakes, produced by Coldcut, were comprised of instrumental hip-hop cuts.\n\nFormerly independent, it was acquired by [l=Concord Music Group, Inc.] on 12 March, 2026.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:109","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":272111,"name":"Concord Music Group, Inc."},"sublabels":[{"id":432612,"name":"Acid Ragga"},{"id":3718,"name":"Ahead Of Our Time"},{"id":733846,"name":"Beat Delete"},{"id":1103,"name":"Big Dada Recordings"},{"id":67959,"name":"Counter Records"},{"id":244774,"name":"Girls Music"},{"id":905737,"name":"IF Music (3)"},{"id":190418,"name":"Motion Audio"},{"id":3014554,"name":"Ninja Cuts"},{"id":629349,"name":"Ninja Rox"},{"id":262808,"name":"Ninja Tone"},{"id":115516,"name